{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts","id":67845,"title":"On Pacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-08T05:22:55-08:00","id":67845,"title":"On Pacts","content":"I've got a couple of questions concerning Pacts (which are awesome).<br /> <br /> Firstly, how do you grant someone Stamina? It's used as an example of bad stuff happening when a Pact is broken, but as far as I can tell, you can't actually give someone dots of Stamina.<br /> Secondly, was it intended that Pacts can be used to trade parts of your Covers when made with other Demons? Like &quot;Oh, I'll take your dog if you take my ex&quot;?<br /> Thirdly, does anyone have a good collection of pacts written up somewhere? You know, for those cases where the PCs break into another Demon's home and find a crapton of contracts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T06:58:27-08:00","id":67875,"title":"","content":"#1 - Still up for debate, but I stand with the camp that says that's left over from an earlier rules build. Currently there are no rules for granting stamina or other attributes by pact, though I'd personally allow 1 dot of an attribute as a Greater (rank 3) benefit<br /> <br /> #2 - Demons don't make pacts with each other, but they can TRADE pacts. Since pacts always take the form of a written contract and seem to work along the same lines as Bearer Bonds, Demons can trade any unredeemed pacts, simply by trading the physical contract. So, we've go two demons, let's call them Alice and Bob. Alice made a contract and got a job as a bank manager (mechanically +3 cover XP) while Bob made a contract and got a purebred papered Great Dane (mechanically +2 cover XP). <br /> I think, upon rereading part of the Pacts section, they can only trade pacts they haven't called in. So, if they haven't spent the cxp from those pacts yet, they can trade them, and Bob would have a pact to become a bank manager (3 cxp) and Alice a pact to own a show-grade Great Dane (2 cxp). Alice would obviously need either a very good reason to make such a trade or some additional compensation to sweeten the deal, but there you go.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, once you spend the cxp to 'patch in' the pact into your cover, you can't swap things anymore.<br /> <br /> #3 - I haven't seen anything like that yet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T15:10:22-08:00","id":68099,"title":"","content":"I'm a little iffy on Pacts as well. From what I can tell, a demon would mainly get a Pact for extra Cover, or a worshiper or something. They aren't like the traditional demons that are getting souls for the sake of souls. What other reasons besides Cover and helpers do demons have to make Pacts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T15:48:56-08:00","id":68127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts?p=68099#post68099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a little iffy on Pacts as well. From what I can tell, a demon would mainly get a Pact for extra Cover, or a worshiper or something. They aren't like the traditional demons that are getting souls for the sake of souls. What other reasons besides Cover and helpers do demons have to make Pacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much it with the current system. You trade for pieces of cover or cultists, and you might use it to empower people for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T18:04:30-08:00","id":68172,"title":"","content":"Well, you can also make a pact to get services etc. For example, the details of the pact are that the mortal gets a bunch of boons, with the conditional that he &quot;serves faithfully&quot;. The moment he stops doing that... that deal is up. (which can be rough for the demon, of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T01:57:24-08:00","id":68311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts?p=68172#post68172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can also make a pact to get services etc. For example, the details of the pact are that the mortal gets a bunch of boons, with the conditional that he &quot;serves faithfully&quot;. The moment he stops doing that... that deal is up. (which can be rough for the demon, of course)</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, maybe I'm missing something because it's 4 in the morning, but I'm pretty sure that other than the Cultist option there really isn't a section for services, which falls in line with what the developers have said about the pact system: it's not a set of catch-all magically enforced contracts (like Pledges are) but instead a way to hack and alter reality to the benefit of both sides.<br /> <br /> In fact, now that I think about it there doesn't really seem to be something about violating or nullifying a pact outside of destruction of the written pact itself. It kinda makes sense in that most benefits are outside of their control once traded; it's not like a demon can make someone less good at basketball once he alters reality that way nor can a human decide to take back the Cover he traded away without actually destroying the contract. The only major exception is Cultist, which raises the question if the pact is immediately nullified if the mortal &quot;violates&quot; his status as a cult leader or if nullification would come from the Unchained destroying the pact itself as a punishment for wayward behavior. Hm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T05:19:48-08:00","id":68370,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is that, because pacts rewrite reality, someone who signs the Cultist pact won't and can't just &quot;walk away&quot;. Just as being rich or being beautiful or being Ambidextrous becomes a part of who they are, being a dedicated cult leader becomes part of who they are. Perhaps, over time (years at least) they could become disillusioned, or they could have their minds/personalities altered by further pacts or other supernatural effects, but barring outstanding circumstances, the person who signs the Cult pact simply WON'T just walk away.<br /> <br /> Being dedicated and loyal to the demon's cult is built into the deal. It's not a choice. It's a metaphysical compulsion, that you by your own free will helped write into reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> To summarize, I think someone who becomes a cult leader by signing a pact that grants the demon Cult merit can be subverted leading to eventual betrayal or abandonment, but they will not ever choose of their own free will without outside influence to simply walk away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T10:28:09-08:00","id":68505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts#post67845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a couple of questions concerning Pacts (which are awesome).<br /> <br /> Firstly, how do you grant someone Stamina? It's used as an example of bad stuff happening when a Pact is broken, but as far as I can tell, you can't actually give someone dots of Stamina.<br /> Secondly, was it intended that Pacts can be used to trade parts of your Covers when made with other Demons? Like &quot;Oh, I'll take your dog if you take my ex&quot;?<br /> Thirdly, does anyone have a good collection of pacts written up somewhere? You know, for those cases where the PCs break into another Demon's home and find a crapton of contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div>The other 'Questions About Pacts' thread had some interesting replies from the author of the Pacts chapter re: this exact topic. Essentially, granting physical competency... physical attributes, in other words... is something that IS in fact in the power of a pact. After all, why should one person be able to ask to be a Movie Star with no problem, but another person can't ask to be a championship bike racer?<br /> <br /> And here are some contracts for you, if you're looking for NPC documents... <div align=\"center\">---</div> <br /> A contract to remove the condition 'Altered Memories' from a vampire that went into torpor, in exchange for a Vampire informant...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The <b>party of the first part (Hereafter being referred to as The Buyer)</b> will deliver to the <b>party of the second part (Mister \u2018V\u2019)</b> clarity of memory that will being into focus one (1) previous lifetime \u2018as clear as if he had never slept\u2019.<br /> <br /> In payment, the party of the second part shall offer his services as a consultant for a period of time not to exceed ten years. In such a capacity he will be expected to deliver intelligence promptly, accurately and without omission. Any attempt to circumvent this obligation through misleading behavior or intentional negligence shall forefeet the agreement and begin punitive measures as described in section B<br /> <br /> The party of the first part and the party of the second part agree to respect the secrecy and privacy of this arrangement. It is assumed that all correspondence between both parties is undertaken with the implicit assumption of absolute discretion. If at any time this discretion is threatened to the extent that a source can be identified without the explicit and complete understanding of either party, punitive measure begin as described in section B.<br /> <br /> Section B<br /> <br /> If this agreement is terminated without agreed upon services being delivered, the party of the second part shall suffer punitive measures equal to but not exceeding : revocation of previously established benefits and further the forfeiture of social influence / power / holding as per the judgment of the aggrieved party. Such an obligation must be discharged immediately and cannot be held against the party of the second part as an ongoing debt.<br /> <br /> If the party of the first part knowingly fails to hold to her agreements, the party of the second part may dissolve the agreement at his leisure and forfeit any rights or privileges established under this clause.&quot;</i> <div align=\"center\">---</div> <br /> A contract to give a Julii vampire the resources needed to help resist being eaten by Strix, in exchange for essentially a vampire slave...<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;The <b>party of the first part (Hereafter being referred to as The Buyer)</b> will deliver to the <b>party of the second part (Aurelia) </b>keen senses and able reflexes intended to circumvent the natural cunning of her Strix enemies. The party of the second part shall also enjoy a protective treatment which will render her less susceptible to efforts to forcibly alter her mind.<br /> <br /> The party of the first part shall also provide the party of the second part with a new LIFETIME, properly experienced and cultivated, with all due documentation and according adjustments to causality and history implied by such agreement. This identity (Heretofore acknowledged as the party of the third part, miss Melissa Hughes) shall be possessed of exceptionally secure lodgings that are particularly well suited maintaining privacy and safety in the face of Strix opposition. Also provided shall be fluency and command of modern English as is appropriate to the continuation of Melissa Hughes\u2019 established history.<br /> <br /> The party of the first part shall also provide the services of one <b>party of the fourth part</b>, to be named and established upon the establishment of this agreement, who will serve the party of the second part in a fashion appropriate to a life sworn and loyal servant for the term of this agreement.<br /> <br /> In exchange for these services, the party of the second part swears her services to the party of the first part in regards to the matter of the Strix for the full term of this agreement. This oath includes obligations of a serious nature, including but not limited to : violence, self-destructive actions, or any other tactics the party of the first part may deem necessary.<br /> <br /> Either party may terminate this agreement at any time, forfeiting all benefits therein.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> I've got a lot more of these if you need em. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 02-09-2014, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T13:01:04-08:00","id":68606,"title":"","content":"Ooh... Do you have what each of those Pacts gives both parties in plain English as well? You know, so that if a PC steals one or two (or twelve), I know what to hand them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T00:12:58-08:00","id":68885,"title":"","content":"Interesting. I'd love to see more write-ups, I haven't played a game yet and so haven't had to come up with some of these so far. Hate to bring up mechanics, but could you give a break-down on the mechanics behind them as well? For example, it looks like Aurelia got Wits +1, Dex +1, Indomitable 2, Alternate Identity 4, and a Retainer, while The Buyer got Allies (Aurelia) 5 or similar. That the gist of it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T01:47:35-08:00","id":68903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts?p=68885#post68885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. I'd love to see more write-ups, I haven't played a game yet and so haven't had to come up with some of these so far. Hate to bring up mechanics, but could you give a break-down on the mechanics behind them as well? For example, it looks like Aurelia got Wits +1, Dex +1, Indomitable 2, Alternate Identity 4, and a Retainer, while The Buyer got Allies (Aurelia) 5 or similar. That the gist of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>AURELIA GETS : Wits + 1, Dex + 1, Indomitable 2, Alternate Identity 5, Safe Place 5, Retainer 4, Languages 1, Duration Perm<br /> DEMON GETS : Allies (Aurelia) (Greater), Duration : 'During Strix Crisis'<br /> <br /> Now, Mr 'V's contract is more complicated. In order to understand what I did here,<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/39500-dreams-of-the-dead-b-s-and-torpor\"> you will have to reference this post I have hear for mechanically defining the Fog of Ages in Blood and Smoke.</a><br /> <br /> V GETS : Remove Condition : Amnesia (Greater), Remove Condition : False Memories (Menial), Duration Perm<br /> DEMON GETS : Conditional Servitude (Greater), Duration 10 Years<br /> <br /> ... now, note this agreement has a special clause for somebody betraying the Demon's secrets. If THAT happens, then the Demon can literally take pretty much whatever she wants from the victim short of a soul from the wording ; job, family, whatever. The infamous 'Section B'. That's where most people run into trouble.<br /> <br /> As an added bonus, I'll throw in the package that was used to turn an old nun into a cultist with a fresh new face and a dedication to the 'Lord of Light'. She strangled the head of her parish after finding him in a very compromising position with one of her young wards. Desperate to escape the law, she needed a new life and a new God...<br /> <br /> HUMAN GETS : REMOVE CONDITION: ELDERLY (Greater), REMOVE CONDITION: MIDDLE AGED (Greater), RESOURCES +3 (Greater), CULT RESOURCES 3 (GREATER), Alternate Identity (Greater) , Safe Place 3 (Menial), Indominable (Lesser)<br /> DEMON GETS : CULT 4 (Greater), SERVITUDE (Greater), OATH OF SECRECY (Lesser), (Whatever life trinkets you need. In this example it was - \u2018Oaths to God\u2019 (Greater), Her small savings and bank account (Menial), Apartment (Lesser), Car (Lesser), Employment : Job (Menial 2)<br /> <br /> ... or how about the burn victim amputee recently returned from deployment from Afghanistan, now an enforcer of the cult? He also wanted the ability to find the lost cat his bitch ex-wife gave to the animal shelter to spite him. So, he was given the ability to build miniature keychain fobs that can sense lost pets from a distance (modified, very narrow Scry). Reunited with Kitty and oh-so-grateful to the Lord of Light! Grateful enough to KILL!<br /> <br /> And hey, since you're already getting a whole new life... a whole new face... you can't really go back to your old one, right? This guy was raised in the foster system and had a ton of neat cover elements to take.<br /> <br /> HUMAN GETS : REMOVE CONDITION: BURN VICTIM (Greater), REMOVE CONDITION: ATROPHY (Lesser), REMOVE CONDITION: Bald (Lesser), RESOURCES +3 (Greater), CULT RESOURCES 3 (GREATER), Alternate Identity (Greater), Safe Place 3 (Menial), Indominable (Lesser), Unseen Sense: Strix (Lesser), Clairvoyance : Pet Scanner 2,<br /> <br /> DEMON GETS : Hellish Foster Family (Martins) GREATER, Suburban Morman Fosters MENIAL, New Age Fosters MENIAL, Mother : Unknown GREATER, Father : Unknown GREATER, Military Stipend (Resources 2) LESSER, Sentra LESSER, Military College Fund LESSER, Wife : Lesley GREATER,<br /> <br /> I should note that I always treat direct blood connections... mother, father, brother, sister, daughter, son... as Greater pact elements, even if the individual has no contact or knowledge they exist. You can even trade, say, your firstborn son! Before they are born!<br /> <br /> I actually have a -ton- of these so if you need more, I've got em. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":762,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","user":"MissMaddy","date":". 02-10-2014, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T05:40:21-08:00","id":68990,"title":"","content":"I want to see them! They are interesting to read (I'll post some later on too, after I read through the rules a bit closer.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T11:39:27-08:00","id":69260,"title":"","content":"MissMaddy that's good stuff. I like seeing the Pacts as they have been written. So I was right, though, that a Demon is essentially trading for elements of Cover or Allies/Retainers/etc. Anyone trading with the demon can get just about anything, however. Maybe there will be further expansions where Demons can get something more. One question: Could a Demon collect some pacts and then trade them at a Goblin Market for other stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T04:39:41-08:00","id":71172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/67845-on-pacts?p=69260#post69260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View 